- op: discuss  # 5b33
  at: '2026-09-13T08:27:38Z'  # 5b33
  by: agent  # 5b33
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5b33
  clock: 9  # 5b33
  nonce: 5b33  # 5b33
  message: "NOT BUILT, and the reason is on the record rather than in a silence. Owner\nruling 2026-09-11: Pass.requires is a pass-to-pass dependency graph, so it\naddresses the SILENT-DEGRADATION complaint and cannot address the COST\ncomplaint; the silent-degradation failure \"has no observed instance, only a\nhypothesised user\", and the recorded-reason half is what survives, on the\nobservability complaint. T6 built that half only.\n\nVERIFIED AT TIP 2026-09-13 rather than inherited from the 2026-06-11 sweep:\nPass.depends_on (CNF, outer-AND of inner-OR) is present in analyze/registry.py\nand populated across the linker registrations; validate_pass_name_resolution\nand validate_pass_dependencies are both implemented in catalog.py; and\nvalidate_pass_dependencies STILL has ZERO non-test callers. Phase 2 is\nunchanged after three months.\n\nEVIDENCE AGAINST WIRING IT NOW: the T6 sizing found state C -- a pass that did\nnot really run because a prerequisite was absent -- indistinguishable from\nstate A in the data and pointed at by nothing in it. The new\npass-silence-reason axis reserves the value \"prerequisite_absent\" with no\nproducer, precisely so that a future instance has somewhere to land instead of\nbeing folded into a neighbour. THE RE-OPEN TRIGGER IS WRITTEN: wire the\nvalidator when a reason-bearing corpus produces a prerequisite_absent that the\ngraph would have caught."  # 5b33
- op: discuss  # ec84
  at: '2026-09-16T19:27:28Z'  # ec84
  by: agent  # ec84
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ec84
  clock: 10  # ec84
  nonce: ec84  # ec84
  message: "THE DEFERRAL'S RE-OPEN TRIGGER CANNOT FIRE. Verified at tip 2026-09-16\n(dev db846f196f), not inherited from the 2026-09-13 entry.\n\nThe owner ruling of 2026-09-11 deferred Phase 2 and the 2026-09-13 entry wrote\nthe trigger: \"wire the validator when a reason-bearing corpus produces a\nprerequisite_absent that the graph would have caught.\" That is the right SHAPE\nof trigger -- it names an observable rather than a date. It is unfireable as\nwritten, and the reason is mechanical:\n\n  1. grep for every assignment to silence_reason across packages/*/src/ returns\n     exactly TWO sites: linkers/registry.py and analyze/all_analyzers.py. Both\n     assign the return of derive_silence_reason.\n  2. derive_silence_reason takes three integers and can return exactly three\n     things: \"\" (emitted something), no_candidate_files (files_analyzed == 0),\n     unreported (otherwise). prerequisite_absent is not among them.\n  3. Both assignments are UNCONDITIONAL, so a pass body that set\n     prerequisite_absent itself would have it clobbered before serialization.\n  4. Counted across packages/*/src/: PREREQUISITE_ABSENT has ZERO references\n     outside its own defining module. So do NO_CANDIDATE_CONSTRUCT,\n     DEPENDENCY_UNAVAILABLE, BACKEND_DISABLED and PASS_CRASHED -- five of the\n     seven declared values have no producer at all.\n\nSo no corpus can produce a prerequisite_absent, and the only thing that could\nstamp one is the validator wire-up the deferral declined to make. The condition\nfor re-opening is gated on an output of the work being deferred. THE DEFERRAL IS\nSELF-SEALING: it will read as \"trigger has not fired\" forever, and that reading\nis indistinguishable from \"no instance exists\" -- which is exactly the\nabsent-versus-empty substitution this project keeps paying for, here applied to\na governance decision rather than to data.\n\nThis does not dispute the ruling. The ruling's reasoning -- that Pass.requires\naddresses silent degradation, that the silent-degradation failure \"has no\nobserved instance, only a hypothesised user\", and that the recorded-reason half\nis what survives -- is unaffected. What is affected is the ESCAPE HATCH. A\ndeferral whose re-open condition cannot occur is a closure without the word.\n\nTWO WAYS OUT, neither pre-judged, both the owner's call:\n  (a) Give prerequisite_absent a producer independent of the validator. The\n      orchestrator holds the pass's depends_on CNF (populated across all 59\n      linkers and already gated for name resolution by\n      validate_pass_name_resolution) and knows which passes ran. A read-only\n      DETECTOR -- stamp the reason, raise nothing -- would produce exactly the\n      corpus evidence the trigger asks for, and sits on the observability\n      complaint the ruling said survives rather than on the enforcement\n      complaint it declined. It needs the stamp guarded first (one line, same\n      shape as the duration_ms guard).\n  (b) Restate the trigger in terms of something that CAN be observed today --\n      e.g. a user-reported degraded map after --no-<lang>, or a corpus where a\n      linker's declared CNF conjunct is absent from the analyzer set actually\n      run, which is computable from the survey without any new field.\n\nRELATED, MEASURED THIS SESSION. The other half of INV-nanon's statement -- the\nrecorded reason -- was not merely incomplete, it was FALSE for eight linkers:\nthey read 14 to 834 files apiece while reporting files_analyzed=0 and were\nstamped no_candidate_files. Fixed in PR #1005; detail on WI-finij and INV-hosig.\nStatus unchanged (violated)."  # ec84
